       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is twice the usual maximum single dose of ibuprofen, which is 800 mg.\n- **Daily total:** 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6400 mg/day. The maximum is 3200 mg/day for inpatients, and 2400 mg/day is the usual ceiling. At 6400 mg/day, the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events goes up substantially.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg by mouth, four times daily** (3200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **600 mg by mouth, four times daily** (2400 mg/day)\n- **400 mg by mouth, every 6 hours** (1600 mg/day, which is 400 mg four times daily)\n- **1600 mg per day in total**, divided into smaller doses\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, tell me the clinical reason and I'll enter it with a note. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
